{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>As I go out of the city</b> According to the plain sense, it is possible to say that Moses would pray in his house, but this time he wanted his hands to be spread out toward the heavens so that the thunder and rain would cease immediately, and it was not possible to do so in the city. Therefore he said, <b>as I go out of the city.</b> And similarly it is stated further (Exodus 9:33), and Moses went out from Pharaoh, out of the city, and at the first instance he said (Exodus 8:25), Behold, I am going out from you. And our Rabbis said (Mekhilta de-Pascha, in the prologue) that he would not pray inside the city because it was full of idols, and all the more so he would not be addressed except outside the city. If so, it must be said that because Pharaoh was now requesting that the hail cease immediately, Moses needed to explain to him that he would have to go out of the city, and afterward he would spread his hands to HaShem and it would cease through his prayer, and this is the truth:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:06.809265899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}